From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qdsp6: release AudioReach graphs across system suspend

An open AudioReach graph keeps the ADSP out of power collapse, so a PCM
left open at suspend, such as a sound still draining or a game's stream,
keeps the ADSP awake for the whole sleep.

Release the stream graphs at device suspend and the port graphs at
component suspend. Drop SNDRV_PCM_INFO_RESUME so userspace re-prepares
the streams after resume.

Resume order matters. The stream (source) graph must be back before its
port (sink) graph, or the DSP consumes the stream without playing it, so
stream graphs reopen at device resume, which the card's device link
orders before the card resumes. Prepared ports are then restored at
component resume, before the DAPM resume event: DPCM does not re-prepare
a BE that was prepared but not running, and codecs may need the port
clock when DAPM powers them. The first prepare after resume leaves a
restored port running rather than stopping it while codecs start.
